<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναξυρίδες</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδων</span>,
			αἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trousers</i> worn by eastern nations, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.5.8
			</span></i>; by the Scythians, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.71
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>; by the Sacae, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.87
			</span></i>, etc.: sg., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> sg. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναξυρίς</span></b> , ἡ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξαλίς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.114
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				838
			</span></i>. (Derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνασύρεσθαι</span>
			by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				22.8
			</span></i>, but really Persian. Wrongly expl. as a head-covering by
				<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.58
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
